properties.statement:
Managing at the hub level (his word 2026-10-18: the hub is the only server) needs every tool to reach a member. Two parts:
(1) A tool that takes no node id can be run on one named member through the hub. Today these act on the hub's own design only:
- loop_status;
- reasoning_report without `claim`, the only walk that roots contested Decisions;
- detect_gaps with no scope;
- describe_schema, find_tools, find_skills, get_skill and get_instructions;
- claim_region and release_claim (the one-PR hold on reflow2's design had to be released through the chat connector);
- usage_report.
(2) A routed reply prefixes EVERY id it returns, so it can be pasted back. Today `premises` come back prefixed, while `assumes`, `conclusion`, `discharges`, error text and reasoning_report's summary lists do not.
Seen in the Arrow trial (H2, H4, H5) and the cogito trial (2026-10-18). This is a gap against req:a-hub-is-an-on-demand-view-over-its-members-designs-and-every-tool-runs-over-it-with-writes-landing-in-the-owning-design ("every ordinary reflow2 tool runs unchanged").
